## Development Standards

### 1. AI Agent Management

**CRITICAL RULE**: All Gemini API interactions MUST be documented in `/docs/AI_AGENTS.md`

When adding/modifying AI features:
1. Define the agent personality/role
2. Select appropriate model (pro vs flash)
3. Justify model selection
4. Document system instructions
5. Specify response format (JSON schema, Markdown, etc.)
6. Update `/docs/AI_AGENTS.md` with the new agent definition

### 2. Service Layer Pattern

All Gemini API calls go through `/services/geminiService.ts`:

```typescript
// Example pattern
export async function generateFeature(input: string): Promise<FeatureResult> {
  const model = genAI.getGenerativeModel({
    model: 'gemini-2.5-pro', // or gemini-2.5-flash
    generationConfig: {
      responseMimeType: "application/json",
      responseSchema: FeatureSchema
    }
  });
  
  const prompt = `Agent personality: ...
  
  Task: ${input}`;
  
  const result = await model.generateContent(prompt);
  return JSON.parse(result.response.text());
}
```

### 3. Component Patterns

Components follow a consistent structure:

```typescript
// components/FeatureName.tsx
import React, { useState } from 'react';
import { FeatureType } from '../types';
import * as geminiService from '../services/geminiService';

interface FeatureNameProps {
  onClose: () => void;
}

export const FeatureName: React.FC<FeatureNameProps> = ({ onClose }) => {
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false);
  const [result, setResult] = useState<FeatureType | null>(null);
  
  const handleGenerate = async () => {
    setLoading(true);
    try {
      const data = await geminiService.generateFeature(input);
      setResult(data);
    } catch (error) {
      console.error('Error:', error);
    } finally {
      setLoading(false);
    }
  };
  
  return (
    <div className="container">
      {/* UI implementation */}
    </div>
  );
};
```

